# Copy to .env.local and fill in. NEVER commit a filled-in copy.
# Production values live in Vercel → Project → Settings → Environment Variables.

# ── UI work without a database ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# Renders auth-gated screens from the mock fixtures in src/lib/mock/, with no
# Supabase project and no login. This is the intended mode for UI work,
# including Builder.io Fusion. Ignored in production builds.
NEXT_PUBLIC_UI_PREVIEW=true

# ── Supabase ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# ORIGIN ONLY. The dashboard sometimes shows the PostgREST endpoint
# (https://<ref>.supabase.co/rest/v1/) — drop that suffix. supabase-js appends
# /rest/v1, /auth/v1 and /storage/v1 itself, so leaving it on 404s every call.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=

# The browser-safe key. Supabase issues these in two generations and the app
# accepts either — set ONE of them, preferring the new format:
#
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY   new format, sb_publishable_…
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY          legacy JWT, eyJ…
#
# Both are safe in the browser and both are fully governed by Row Level
# Security — for WRITES as well as reads. Neither is read-only: they can
# insert, update and delete anywhere a policy permits.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# ⚠ SERVER-ONLY. Bypasses Row Level Security entirely: a query made with this
# key can read and write every student record regardless of who is logged in.
# Treat a leak as a full database compromise and rotate immediately.
# Never expose it to the browser, and never add it to a Builder.io environment.
# Same two generations; set ONE, preferring the new format:
#
#   SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY          new format, sb_secret_…
#   SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY    legacy JWT, eyJ…
#
# Only the Admin staff-invite flow needs it. Sign-in, sign-out and password
# reset all work without it.
SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY=
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# ── Builder.io ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Not used in v1: Fusion generates code into this repo, so the app has no
# runtime dependency on Builder. Only needed if the Builder SDK is ever added
# (e.g. for the Phase 2 marketing site — PRD §11).
# NEXT_PUBLIC_BUILDER_API_KEY=
# BUILDER_PRIVATE_KEY=          # ⚠ server-only
